<document xmlns="http://cnx.rice.edu/cnxml" xmlns:m="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML">
  <title>3.3.5: Practice</title>
  <metadata xmlns:md="http://cnx.rice.edu/mdml">
    <md:content-id>m00742</md:content-id>
    <md:title>3.3.5: Practice</md:title>
    <md:uuid>bd9b19b4-56a8-48d2-a705-7495dab132e0</md:uuid>
  </metadata>
  <content>
    <section>
      <para dir="ltr">Complete the following questions to practice the skills you have learned in this lesson.</para>
      <section class="check-understanding">
        <exercise data-content-id="9196cbfd-6686-44e7-b947-f95b2d634560" class="multiple-choice">
          <problem>
            <para>Using the following information, find the residual for each of the coordinate pairs, \((x,y)\) in 1 - 6.</para>
            <para>
              <quote>A line of best fit for a data set is \(y=1.1x+3.4\). </quote>
            </para>
            <para>\((5,8.8)\)</para>
          </problem>
          <solution>
            <para>Correct! \(-0.1\)</para>
            <para>Try again. Revisit activity 3.3.2.</para>
            <para>The correct answer is \(-0.1\). </para>
            <para>\(y = 1.1x + 3.4\\
        y = 1.1(5) + 3.4\\
        y = 8.9\\
        8.8 − 8.9 = −0.1\)</para>
          </solution>
        </exercise>
        <exercise data-content-id="41ea8366-511c-46f1-9248-bcdf9d8ae799" class="multiple-choice">
          <problem>
            <para>\((2.5,5.95)\)</para>
          </problem>
          <solution>
            <para>Correct! \(-0.2\)</para>
            <para>Try again. Revisit activity 3.3.2.</para>
            <para>The correct answer is \(-0.2\).
      </para>
            <para>\(y = 1.1x + 3.4\\
        y = 1.1(2.5) + 3.4\\
        y = 6.15\\
        5.95 − 6.15 = −0.2\)</para>
          </solution>
        </exercise>
        <exercise data-content-id="796342e5-4c65-41f0-81ad-1a55e4a44250" class="multiple-choice">
          <problem>
            <para>\((0,3.72)\)</para>
          </problem>
          <solution>
            <para>Correct! 0.32</para>
            <para>Try again. Revisit activity 3.3.2.</para>
            <para>The correct answer is 0.32.
      </para>
            <para>\(y = 1.1x + 3.4\\
        y = 1.1(0) + 3.4\\
        y = 3.4\\
        3.72 − 3.4 = 0.32\)</para>
          </solution>
        </exercise>
        <exercise data-content-id="43d436cf-1bfb-4538-8998-9e2746249a2a" class="multiple-choice">
          <problem>
            <para>\((1.5,5.05)\)</para>
          </problem>
          <solution>
            <para>Correct!  0</para>
            <para>Try again. Revisit activity 3.3.2.</para>
            <para>The correct answer is 0.
      </para>
            <para>\(y = 1.1x + 3.4\\
        y = 1.1(1.5) + 3.4\\
        y = 5.05\\
        5.05 − 5.05 = 0\)</para>
          </solution>
        </exercise>
        <exercise data-content-id="7e052619-fa5c-4e8e-86a9-4b2d4a6147fe" class="multiple-choice">
          <problem>
            <para>\((-3,0)\)</para>
          </problem>
          <solution>
            <para>Correct! \(-0.1\)</para>
            <para>Try again. Revisit activity 3.3.2.</para>
            <para>The correct answer is \(-0.1\).
      </para>
            <para>\(y = 1.1x + 3.4\\
        y = 1.1(−3) + 3.4\\
        y = 0.1\\
        0 − 0.1 = −0.1\)</para>
          </solution>
        </exercise>
        <exercise data-content-id="6c00c18c-7142-4177-8446-3f86054d3eb9" class="multiple-choice">
          <problem>
            <para>\((-5,-4.86)\)</para>
          </problem>
          <solution>
            <para>Correct! \(-2.76\)</para>
            <para>Try again. Revisit activity 3.3.2.</para>
            <para>The correct answer is \(-2.76\).
      </para>
            <para>\(y = 1.1x + 3.4\\
        y = 1.1(−5) + 3.4\\
        y = −2.1\\
        −4.86 − (−2.1) = −2.76\)</para>
          </solution>
        </exercise>
      </section>
      <section class="check-understanding">
        <exercise data-content-id="eb973c60-4a19-4cee-8d55-46c103eaa674" class="multiple-choice">
          <problem>
            <para>7. In the scatter plot below, the length of fish and the age of the fish are shown. The residual for the fish that is 2 years old and 100 mm long is 8.06 mm.</para>
            <para>
              <figure>
                <media alt="A SCATTER PLOT THAT SHOWS AGE OF FISH IN YEARS ON THE X-AXIS AND LENGTH OF FISH IN MILLIMETERS ON THE Y-AXIS. A LINE OF BEST FIT IS DRAWN, AND THE POINT (2, 100) IS LABELED.">
                  <image mime-type="image/svg+xml" src="../../media/Algebra-1_03_05_10_01.svg"/>
                </media>
              </figure>
            </para>
            <para>What does this residual mean?</para>
          </problem>
          <solution>
            <para>Correct! The actual fish at 2 years old is about 8 mm longer than the linear model estimates.
      </para>
            <para>Try again. Revisit activities 3.3.2 – 3.3.3.</para>
            <para>Compare your answer: The actual fish at 2 years old is about 8 mm longer than the linear model estimates.
      </para>
          </solution>
        </exercise>
      </section>
      <section class="check-understanding">
        <exercise data-content-id="cdacea9f-490b-4fbe-97b6-0cea60ee4cbc" class="multiple-choice">
          <problem>
            <para>Use the following information to answer 8 - 11.</para>
            <para>
              <quote>Four athletes on a track team are comparing their personal bests in the 100-meter and 200-meter events. A table of their best times is shown below. </quote>
              <quote>The line of best fit has an equation of \(y= 1.5115x + 7.526\), where \(x\) represents the 100-meter time and \(y\) represents the 200-meter time.
        </quote>
            </para>
            <para>What is the residual for athlete number 1?</para>
          </problem>
          <solution>
            <para>Correct! \(-0.42\)</para>
            <para>Try again. Revisit activity 3.3.2.</para>
            <para>Compare your answer: \(-0.42\). </para>
            <para>\(y = 1.5115x + 7.526\\
        y = 1.5115(12.95) + 7.526\\
        y = 27.10\\
        26.68 − 27.10 = −0.42\)</para>
          </solution>
        </exercise>
        <exercise data-content-id="3ba4d02e-7eba-4bfd-bf53-83fddd611ca9" class="multiple-choice">
          <problem>
            <para>What is the residual for athlete number 2?</para>
          </problem>
          <solution>
            <para>Correct! 1.08</para>
            <para>Try again. Revisit activity 3.3.2.</para>
            <para>Compare your answer: 1.08. </para>
            <para>\(y = 1.5115x + 7.526\\
        y = 1.5115(13.81) + 7.526\\
        y = 28.40\\
        29.48 − 28.40 = 1.08\)</para>
          </solution>
        </exercise>
        <exercise data-content-id="b418d045-c6ee-4f99-b053-064adabb94ca" class="multiple-choice">
          <problem>
            <para>What is the residual for athlete number 3?</para>
          </problem>
          <solution>
            <para>Correct! \(-1.57\)</para>
            <para>Try again. Revisit activity 3.3.2.</para>
            <para>Compare your answer: \(-1.57\). </para>
            <para>\(y = 1.5115x + 7.526\\
        y = 1.5115(14.66) + 7.526\\
        y = 29.68\\
        28.11 − 29.68 = −1.57\)</para>
          </solution>
        </exercise>
        <exercise data-content-id="0068eba3-1a1b-49b0-ad19-acc695d72437" class="multiple-choice">
          <problem>
            <para>What is the residual for athlete number 4?</para>
          </problem>
          <solution>
            <para>Correct! 0.91</para>
            <para>Try again. Revisit activity 3.3.2.</para>
            <para>Compare your answer: 0.91. </para>
            <para>\(y = 1.5115x + 7.526\\
        y = 1.5115(14.88) + 7.526\\
        y = 30.02\\
        30.93 − 30.02 = 0.91\)</para>
          </solution>
        </exercise>
      </section>
      <section class="check-understanding">
        <exercise data-content-id="d8d7b36d-05a3-466c-883b-73fecef80ce2" class="multiple-choice">
          <problem>
            <para>12. The curb weight of a car is the weight of the car without luggage or passengers. The scatter plot below shows the curb weight, in pounds, of 5 cars and their fuel efficiency, in miles per gallon.</para>
            <div>
              <para>Will the residual for 25.33 be a positive or negative value?</para>
            </div>
            <para>
              <figure>
                <media alt="A SCATTER PLOT WITH CURB WEIGHT IN HUNDREDS OF POUNDS ON THE X-AXIS AND FUEL EFFICIENCY IN MILES PER GALLON ON THE Y-AXIS. A LINE OF BEST FIT IS DRAWN. FOUR POINTS ARE ABOVE THE LINE AND ONE POINT IS BELOW.">
                  <image mime-type="image/jpeg" src="../../media/Algebra-1_03_05_10_02.jpg"/>
                </media>
              </figure>
            </para>
          </problem>
          <solution>
            <para>Correct! The residual is positive because it is above the line.</para>
            <para>Try again. Revisit activities 3.3.3 – 3.3.4.</para>
            <para>Compare your answer: the residual is positive because it is above the line. </para>
          </solution>
        </exercise>
      </section>
    </section>
  </content>
</document>
